":\"The list's position in the room's sequence: exactly one greater than the last list the room signed. A host accepts only a list whose sequence is above the one it holds, which is what stops a host, a relayer or an attacker holding an old list from rolling the room's withdrawals back.\"},\"issuedAt\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"date-time\",\"description\":\"When the room signed this list.\"},\"entries\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"maxItems\":4096,\"items\":{\"$ref\":\"#/$defs/RevocationEntry\"},\"description\":\"Every withdrawal still in force, in the order the room made them. Empty is valid: a room that has revoked nothing, or whose every entry has lapsed, can still state its sequence.\"},\"proof\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"description\":\"The room's Data Integrity proof over every other member, made with a key the room's DID document lists for `assertionMethod`.\"}}},\"RevocationEntry\":{\"title\":\"RevocationEntry\",\"description\":\"One withdrawal in a `RevocationList`, discriminated by `kind`.\\n\\n  - `credential` withdraws one credential, named by its `id`. It matches the membership credential or any authority link whose `id` equals `credentialId`.\\n  - `subject` withdraws a party: every credential the room's chain gave them **before** `revokedAt`. It matches the membership credential or any authority link whose `credentialSubject` id **or** `issuer` is `subject` and whose `validFrom` is earlier than `revokedAt`. Matching the issuer as well as the subject withdraws what the party delegated before their removal, which no re-admission revives. A credential carrying no `validFrom` is treated as issued before every entry.\\n  - `room` withdraws every credential whose `validFrom` is earlier than `revokedAt`, whoever holds it. It is how a room resets access — after a compromise, or on a `private` room, where naming a party would disclose who was a member.\\n\\n**Keyed on time, so a party can come back.** A `subject` or `room` entry withdraws what was issued before it and nothing after, so a room that re-admits a removed party issues fresh credentials and they verify. A `credential` entry is permanent for that one credential, which nobody re-issues.\\n\\n**Tiers.** On a `private` room a host MUST refuse a list carrying a `credential` or `subject` entry: a presentation there withholds the credential and its subject, so such an entry is one the host cannot apply and a disclosure of who was in the room. Only `room` entries are permitted, and a host serving a `private` room MUST refuse any presentation for which it cannot establish that no credential in it has a `validFrom` earlier than the latest `room` entry's `revokedAt`.\",\"oneOf\":[{\"$ref\":\"#/$defs/CredentialRevocation\"},{\"$ref\":\"#/$defs/SubjectRevocation\"},{\"$ref\":\"#/$defs/RoomRevocation\"}]},\"RoomRevocation\":{\"title\":\"RoomRevocation\",\"type\":\"object\",\"additionalProperties\":false,\"required\":[\"kind\",\"revokedAt\"],\"description\":\"Withdraws every credential whose `validFrom` is earlier than `revokedAt`, whoever holds it.\",\"properties\":{\"kind\":{\"const\":\"room\"},\"revokedAt\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"date-time\",\"description\":\"When the room made this withdrawal.\"},\"until\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"date-time\",\"description\":\"OPTIONAL. After this instant every credential the entry matches has expired anyway, so a host MAY discard the entry and the room MAY omit it from later lists. Absent means the entry is kept for as long as the room keeps a list.\"}}},\"SubjectRevocation\":{\"title\":\"SubjectRevocation\",\"type\":\"object\",\"additionalProperties\":false,\"required\":[\"kind\",\"subject\",\"revokedAt\"],\"description\":\"Withdraws a party: every credential naming them as subject or issuer whose `validFrom` is earlier than `revokedAt`.\",\"properties\":{\"kind\":{\"const\":\"subject\"},\"subject\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"pattern\":\"^did:\",\"maxLength\":2048,\"description\":\"The party withdrawn. Never the room itself.\"},\"revokedAt\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"date-time\",\"description\":\"When the room made this withdrawal.\"},\"until\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"date-time\",\"description\":\"OPTIONAL. After this instant every credential the entry matches has expired anyway, so a host MAY discard the entry and the room MAY omit it from later lists. Absent means the entry is kept for as long as the room keeps a list.\"}}},\"CredentialRevocation\":{\"title\":\"CredentialRevocation\",\"type\":\"object\",\"additionalProperties\":false,\"required\":[\"kind\",\"credentialId\",\"revokedAt\"],\"description\":\"Withdraws one credential — a membership credential or any authority link — by its `id`.\",\"properties\":{\"kind\":{\"const\":\"credential\"},\"credentialId\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"minLength\":1,\"maxLength\":2048,\"description\":\"The `id` of the credential withdrawn, as `rooms/owner/issue-authority` and `rooms/owner/issue-membership` return it, or as an attenuated credential carries it.\"},\"revokedAt\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"date-time\",\"description\":\"When the room made this withdrawal.\"},\"until\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"format\":\"date-time\",\"description\":\"OPTIONAL. After this instant every credential the entry matches has expired anyway, so a host MAY discard the entry and the room MAY omit it from later lists. Absent means the entry is kept for as long as the room keeps a list.\"}}}}}"

// Spec is the SPEC §7.2 policy for the request variant, taken from this
// specification's front matter. Pass it to trusttasks.ConsumeInbound — items 5b,
// 7 and 8 are per-specification and cannot be derived from the document alone,
// and item 2 needs the schema it carries.
var Spec = trusttasks.SpecPolicy{
	TypeURI:             TypeURI,
	IsBearer:            false,
	IsProofRequired:     true,
	IsRecipientRequired: true,
	IsIssuedAtRequired:  true,
	PayloadSchema:       PayloadSchemaJSON,
}

// ResponseSpec is the SPEC §7.2 policy for the success-response variant.
// IsRecipientRequired tracks the *issuer* party's requirement, because a response
// swaps the parties (§7.3 item 5).
var ResponseSpec = trusttasks.SpecPolicy{
	TypeURI:             ResponseTypeURI,
	IsBearer:            false,
	IsProofRequired:     true,
	IsRecipientRequired: true,
	IsIssuedAtRequired:  true,
	PayloadSchema:       ResponsePayloadSchemaJSON,
}
